# Ion-speed scan on the W2 rho2M angled ladder: DIAGNOSIS (post-default), 2026-10-13.
#
# WHAT IT ASKS. FRESH_LOOK §13-14: the drifting ion in Ar/iC4H10 95/5 is a hydrocarbon
# fragment, not the Ar+ the S3 emitter hardcodes. Measured low-field mobilities in 95 % Ar
# (Cortez et al., JINST 14 P04010) are K0 1.74 (C8Hn+) and 2.08 (C4Hn+) against Ar+ 1.21
# at the gap's ~124-133 Td, i.e. x1.44 / x1.72; det0 (6 mm gap, He-calibrated shaper)
# and June det3 at the noise-ACF shaper want T ~ 140-220 ns, i.e. x1.6-2.5.
# --ion-speed-scale time-compresses the measured S3 ion template (exact, §7.5).
#
#   s 1.46 : C8Hn+  (t90 212 ns)
#   s 1.75 : C4Hn+  (t90 177 ns)
#   s 2.45 : the §10.2 best fit at 166 ns shaping (t90 127 ns)
#
# Same as stageBC_w2_angled.sub otherwise (corrected FEU 07 noise, angled clusters,
# 180 ns chain shaper, measured template, f_ion 0.9006).
#
# PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTION (written 2026-10-13 before submission), X-view peak-strip
# 10-90 % rise medians, data 181 ns (10.7 deg) / 166 ns (20 deg); chain at s = 1 was
# 247 / 231-ish:
#   s 1.46 -> rise falls by 25-40 ns, still 30-50 ns above data;
#   s 1.75 -> falls by 40-55 ns, 15-35 ns above data;
#   s 2.45 -> falls by 55-75 ns, within ~15 ns of data at 10-20 deg.
#   Peak amplitude per event rises x1.15-1.30 at 10-20 deg, ~x1.08 vertical.
# FALSIFIERS: (a) s 2.45 still > 25 ns above data at both angles -> ion speed alone
#   cannot close the rise at the chain's 180 ns shaper; the shaper question (He says
#   130-150, noise ACF 166) becomes decisive. (b) Rise moves < 15 ns between s 1 and
#   s 2.45 -> the chain's rise floor is not the ion term, contradicting
#   DIAGNOSIS_noions (2026-08-09).
universe                = vanilla
executable              = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/run_stageBC_w2.sh
log                     = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/w2.log
request_cpus            = 4
request_memory          = 16000
request_disk            = 12000000
+JobFlavour             = "workday"
MY.SendCredential       = true
environment             = "OMP_NUM_THREADS=4"
arguments               = "rho2M ionspeed$(tag)_$(ang) /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/calib/noise_det3_satscan_feu07.json /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/clusters_ang/mx17_muons_3k_ang_$(ang)_t0.root '--ion-speed-scale $(s)'"
output                  = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/stageBC_ionspeed$(tag)_$(ang).out
error                   = /afs/cern.ch/work/d/dneff/mx17_s1/logs/stageBC_ionspeed$(tag)_$(ang).err
queue tag, s, ang from (
146, 1.46, th00
146, 1.46, thx10
146, 1.46, thx20
175, 1.75, th00
175, 1.75, thx10
175, 1.75, thx20
245, 2.45, th00
245, 2.45, thx10
245, 2.45, thx20
)
